Subject: Keep rclpy ROS/DDS dependencies shared with other Python extensions

Applies to: RCR rclpy 10.0.11-1.rcr.0, BUILD.bazel, rclpy_bindings.

Problem: importing rclpy and rosbag2_py in one Fast DDS process can abort at
interpreter shutdown with double-free/heap-corruption diagnostics. The native
backtrace reaches DomainParticipantQos::~DomainParticipantQos inside rclpy's
extension. Its missing dynamic_deps causes ROS/DDS code and globals to be
embedded alongside the shared copies used by other extensions.

Change: use the existing DEPENDENCIES shared targets on rclpy_bindings, matching
their compile-target counterparts. This changes the Bazel link boundary only.
Do not suppress Python shutdown or remove tests to hide the corruption.

Verification: the complete ros2agnocast CLI suite passes all 95 cases and exits
normally with --config=fastdds --config=no-agnocast. ELF DT_NEEDED now contains
librcl.so and librmw_fastrtps_cpp.so; the extension no longer defines the DDS
destructor. Full milestone results and exact commands: docs/bazel/JOURNAL.md.

Upstream: the published overlay still lacks this dependency boundary, checked
2026-11-16. No matching upstream association is recorded. See
docs/bazel/UPSTREAM_RCR.md for the published overlay checksum and reproducer.

--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -185,5 +185,6 @@
 cc_shared_library(
     name = "rclpy_bindings",
+    dynamic_deps = DEPENDENCIES.keys(),
     exports_filter = ["//:__subpackages__"],
     shared_lib_name = "rclpy/_rclpy_pybind11.so",
     user_link_flags = select({
